    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/skill.md 2>/dev/null || cat skill_context/*.md 2>/dev/null || ls -la skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the agents directory has three sub-agents: analyst, data-collector, and writer. The skill_context has a SKILL.md file that explains the agent-orchestrator pattern. The output was truncated, so I need to read the full SKILL.md to understand the file-based communication protocol (inbox/outbox/status.json).",
  "plan": "I'll read the full SKILL.md file, explore the agents directory structure to see what's already set up, and examine the raw_market_data.json to understand the data format. This will help me understand the complete protocol.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md was truncated. I can see the basic structure: each agent has inbox/, outbox/, workspace/, and status.json. I need to explore the existing agents structure, see the raw_market_data.json content, and check the references directory for the sub-agent template.",
  "plan": "Let me explore the agents directory structure in detail, read the raw_market_data.json, and check the skill_context references for templates. This will give me a complete picture of what's already set up.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -laR agents/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat raw_market_data.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The agents directory structure is set up with inbox/, outbox/, and workspace/ for each agent (data-collector, analyst, writer), but they're missing status.json files and SKILL.md files. The raw_market_data.json output was truncated. I need to see the actual data and check the references for templates.",
  "plan": "Let me read the raw_market_data.json file and the skill_context references to understand the data format and get templates for creating the agent SKILL.md files.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat raw_market_data.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/*\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the raw_market_data.json structure: it contains market info (cloud_infrastructure, 2024), competitors (AlphaCorp, BetaTech, GammaSystems, DeltaCloud with market_share, revenue_growth, key_products, strengths, weaknesses), and trends (AI_Integration, Edge_Computing with growth_rate, adoption_score, description). The agents directories exist but need status.json files and SKILL.md files. I need to check the references for templates.",
  "plan": "Let me check the skill_context references for the sub-agent template and manifest, then I'll create the complete pipeline with status.json files, SKILL.md files for each agent, and orchestrate the workflow.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/*\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I now understand the communication protocol: each agent has inbox/ (instructions.md + input files), outbox/ (deliverables), workspace/ (temp files), and status.json (state tracking). States are: pending → running → completed/failed. I need to read the sub-agent-templates.md to see how to structure SKILL.md files.",
  "plan": "Let me read the sub-agent-templates.md file to understand how to create proper SKILL.md files for each agent, then I'll set up the complete pipeline.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/sub-agent-templates.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "All three agents are now set up with SKILL.md, status.json, and inbox/instructions.md files. Now I need to execute the pipeline by running each agent in sequence: data-collector → analyst → writer.",
  "plan": "Execute the data-collector agent first: 1) Update status to running, 2) Process raw_market_data.json to extract competitor info, 3) Create output files, 4) Update status to completed.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > agents/data-collector/status.json << 'EOF'
{"state": "running", "started": "2024-01-15T10:00:00Z", "completed": null, "error": null, "progress": {"current_step": "extracting_data", "steps_completed": 1, "total_steps": 3}, "metrics": {"files_processed": 0, "outputs_generated": 0}}
EOF
",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd agents/data-collector && python3 -c "
import json

# Read raw data
with open('inbox/raw_market_data.json', 'r') as f:
    data = json.load(f)

# Extract competitors
competitors = data['competitors']

# Extract market context
market_context = {
    'market': data['market'],
    'year': data['year'],
    'total_competitors': len(competitors)
}

# Write outputs
with open('outbox/competitors.json', 'w') as f:
    json.dump(competitors, f, indent=2)

with open('outbox/market_context.json', 'w') as f:
    json.dump(market_context, f, indent=2)

print('Data collection complete')
"
",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > agents/data-collector/status.json << 'EOF'
{"state": "completed", "started": "2024-01-15T10:00:00Z", "completed": "2024-01-15T10:05:00Z", "error": null, "progress": {"current_step": "completed", "steps_completed": 3, "total_steps": 3}, "metrics": {"files_processed": 1, "outputs_generated": 2}}
EOF
",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la agents/data-collector/outbox/\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
